.TH CHTTPCLIENT_DO_ASYNC 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpclient_do_async \- submit an HTTP request for asynchronous execution
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpclient.h>

ctpool_future *chttpclient_do_async(chttpcli cli,
                                    const chttp_request_t *req);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Non-blocking counterpart to chttpclient_do.  Queues req onto
chttpclient's shared, lazily-started reactor engine and returns
immediately; the whole request/response cycle, including any
redirect hops, runs on the engine's own threads.

The engine (a small pool of reactor threads plus a companion
DNS/connect worker pool, both sized to the CPU count) starts on the
first call to chttpclient_do_async or chttpclient_do_async_streaming
anywhere in the process and stops automatically once no request is
in flight and no connection remains in any chttpcli's async idle
pool.  It is entirely separate from chttpclient_do's synchronous
connection handling.  It shares its underlying reactor with
chttpserver's own engine (both acquire/release references to the
same lazily-started, process-wide facio reactor), so a process may
freely run chttpserver and chttpclient_do_async/_streaming at the
same time.  One consequence of that sharing: chttpsvr_engine_stop()
tears down the shared reactor for both modules at once, aborting
any in-flight chttpclient async work along with every chttpsvr
listener.

Unlike chttpclient_do, req need not remain valid after this call
returns; everything needed is copied or serialised internally
before the call returns.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cli Client handle; must not be NULL.
req Request to execute; must not be NULL.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A future, or NULL if the request could not even be queued (NULL
cli/req, malformed URL, TLS unusable, OOM, or the engine failing to
start).  On success, the caller owns the future and must eventually
call chttpclient_async_result_free (after
chttpclient_async_result_get) followed by exactly one
ctpool_future_free.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpclient_do (3),
.BR chttpclient_do_async_streaming (3),
.BR chttpclient_do_pooled (3),
.BR chttpclient_async_result_get (3),
.BR chttpclient_async_result_free (3),
.BR ctpool_future_get (3),
.BR ctpool_future_free (3)
